☠ MORTAL FRETS — The Fretboard Slayer
A retro arcade-style guitar fretboard training game inspired by Mortal Kombat. Train your fretboard knowledge across 4 identification modes, compete on a global leaderboard, and earn the FLAWLESS VICTORY.
Game Modes
All modes play as rounds of 10 questions. Score = total errors (fewer is better). Tiebreaker: fastest time.
ModeWhat you seeWhat you doNote IDA dot on the fretboard (frets 0–12, all strings)Press the correct note nameInterval IDTwo dots — R (root, red) and interval note within ±3 frets/±2 stringsPress the correct interval (m2 → P8)Chord IDChord voicing within ±2 frets/±2 strings of root, one note per stringPress the correct chord typeScale IDFull scale pattern in a 5-fret box, R = rootPress the correct scale name
Construction modes (v2.0) — coming soon.
Rules

Wrong answer → stay on the same question, retry. Timer keeps running.
Mercy ☠ → activates after 2 wrong answers on the same question. Hold to reveal the answer; release to hide it and retry. Resets each new question.
Variety → same note/interval/chord/scale type appears at most twice per round; exact same question never repeats.
Notation → toggle A-B-C or Do-Re-Mi at any time.
Box selection → Chord ID and Scale ID let you work on a fixed 5-fret box or 💀 KHAOS (random box each question).

Scoring
ErrorsResult0⚡ FLAWLESS VICTORY1–2EXCELLENT FIGHTER3–5SKILLED WARRIOR6–10FIGHT HARDER11–19FINISH HIM20+FATALITY
Deploy on GitHub Pages

Create a public repo on GitHub
Upload mortal_frets.html renamed as index.html
Go to Settings → Pages → Source: Deploy from branch → main → / (root)
Live at https://yourusername.github.io/mortal-frets/ within 1–2 minutes

Global Leaderboard (Firebase)
By default scores are saved in localStorage (local, per-browser). See the Firebase setup section in the repo or follow the in-file instructions to enable a real global leaderboard.
Tech Stack
Pure HTML/CSS/JavaScript — no framework, no build step · Web Audio API · SVG fretboard · Firebase Realtime Database (optional) · Press Start 2P + Rajdhani via Google Fonts
Music Theory Coverage
Notes: all 12 chromatic, frets 0–12, all 6 strings (standard tuning E A D G B e)
Intervals: m2 · M2 · m3 · M3 · P4 · TT · P5 · m6 · M6 · m7 · M7 · P8
Chords: Maj · min · Aug · Dim · Maj7 · Dom7 · min7 · ø7 · °7
Scales: Major · Natural Minor · Harmonic Minor · Melodic Minor · Whole-Half Dim · Half-Whole Dim
